title: Genesis 13 – Toward Sodom
description: A study in Genesis 13: Abram and Lot part ways, Lot pitches his tent toward Sodom, and God renews His promise to Abram and his seed, which is Christ.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-13-toward-sodom.html

=== Introduction
--- Toward Sodom [title]
overline: A study in Genesis 13
sub: Lot’s choice, and the promise to Abram renewed.
refs: Genesis 13:10-12
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== Back to the altar
--- Unto the place of the altar
scripture: Genesis 13:1-4 | mark: Unto the place of the altar, which he had made there at the first
p: Chapter 13 brings Abram and Sarai and his nephew Lot back to the land of Canaan, back to where Abram called upon the name of the {Lord}, near Bethel, on the west bank of the Jordan, in the area of Jerusalem and Bethlehem. There, scripture reminds us, he had built an altar. [[Genesis 12:8]]

--- Let there be no strife
scripture: Genesis 13:5-9 | mark: Let there be no strife, I pray thee, between me and thee
p: Because of the greatness of his herds and Lot’s, and growing contention between each other’s herdsmen, Abram gives Lot his choice of grazing land.

=== Lot’s choice
--- As the garden of the Lord
heading: Even as the garden of the {Lord}
scripture: Genesis 13:10-13 | mark: even as the garden of the LORD, like the land of Egypt; pitched his tent toward Sodom; wicked and sinners before the LORD exceedingly
p: Lot chooses the plain of Jordan, just above what’s called the Dead Sea today. Seeing there was much water and vegetation, *even as the garden of the {Lord}, like the land of Egypt*, and so enticed, he pitches his tent there to the east, toward Sodom.

--- We pitch our tents toward Sodom
lead: There’s many times in life we are given a choice like this, and choosing from ease or greed or comfort, we pitch our tents toward Sodom, toward wickedness and sin.
p: Thinking about the times in my life where, rather than do what needed to be done to end strife, or to get through problems with myself or others, I instead pitched my tent toward Sodom.
- Trusting in a perceived gain over doing what was right.
- Choosing selfishly, rather than in grace.
- Lured by the promise of worldly and carnal gains, ignoring the sin of those around me, and so ignoring my own.

--- Throwing my lot in
panel-warn: Like just Lot | Who separated himself from righteous Abram and dwelled among the men of Sodom, throwing my lot (👀) in with men who were *wicked and sinners before the {Lord} exceedingly*. [[2 Peter 2:7-8]]
panel-warn: Backsliding | This temptation to choose the easy path leads to backsliding and often to destruction. To years and talents and influence wasted that could have been in service to God and being a blessing to my people.
refs: 1 John 2:15-17; 2 Corinthians 6:17

=== The promise renewed
--- After that Lot was separated
heading: After that Lot was separated
scripture: Genesis 13:14-17 | mark: after that Lot was separated from him; to thee will I give it, and to thy seed for ever; as the dust of the earth
callout: **Pay attention to the order of events here.** It is after Lot chooses to pitch his tent toward Sodom that God appears to Abram and gives him additional blessings, reinforcing His promise. This is how it usually works.

--- And to thy seed, which is Christ
big: Galatians 3:16 | mark: And to thy seed, which is Christ
- Christ is the answer to the promises, kept by God. Jesus is the seed through whom all nations are blessed.
- It is in Jesus that the promised land is given for ever, to those who believe and call upon the name of the {Lord}. [[Hebrews 11:13-16]]
- It is in this seed that Abram can be said to have fathered a people too numerous to count, saved sons of God. [[Galatians 3:29]]

--- An altar in Mamre
scripture: Genesis 13:18 | mark: built there an altar unto the LORD
p: Abram settles down in Hebron and the plains of Mamre. The Oak of Abraham, in modern day Hebron along the plains of Mamre on the West Bank, is said to be thousands of years old. Traditions of men claimed that when it died, it would signify the birth of the antichrist. It died in 1996.

=== Close
--- Where is your tent pitched? [title]
overline: Genesis 13
point: Abram returned to the altar | Back to where he first called upon the name of the {Lord}.
point: Lot chose by sight | Well watered, like Egypt, toward Sodom.
point: God renewed the promise | After the separation, the land and the seed as the dust of the earth.
point: The seed is Christ | In Him the promise is kept to all who believe.

